  m_Name: 1819
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: British Establish Singapore 1819
  info: "Sir Stamford Raffles, an agent of the British East India Company, arrives
    in Singapore and quickly recognizes its strategic importance for controlling
    regional trade and countering Dutch influence. Raffles negotiates with Sultan
    Hussein Shah of Johor and the Temenggong of Johor to establish a British trading
    post. Singapore\u2019s declaration as a free port attracts merchants from across
    Asia, including Chinese, Indian, Malay, and Arab traders, transforming it into
    a vibrant and diverse trading hub."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5115cf0708ef747f380fc999d1132c61, type: 3}
